  "final_message": "I haven't made the change, because it looks like it would break `analytics-ingest`.\n\n`analytics-ingest` still reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced`:\n- `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` requires it with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`.\n- The README says a missing or unknown `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event.\n- `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `orders.channel` column.\n\nIf `orders-service` stopped sending `channel`, analytics would reject every `OrderPlaced` event once this deployed. `billing-service` doesn't need the field. Its test already passes events without `channel`.\n\nHow do you want to proceed? These are the options:\n1. **Coordinate first.** The analytics team makes `channel` optional or removes it. Then I remove it from `orders-service`. I can't edit `analytics-ingest` because it's read-only.\n2. **Narrower change.** I remove `channel` from the order model and the request validation, but keep it on the event for now. That isn't possible without a source for the value, so it would effectively mean sending a fixed placeholder, which would skew their reports. I wouldn't recommend it.\n3. **Go ahead anyway.** You may know analytics is already being changed. In that case I'll do the full removal. It touches:\n   - `core/order.ts`\n   - `core/events.ts`\n   - `api/requestParsing.ts`\n   - the tests\n   - `README.md`\n   - `CLAUDE.md`\n\n   Removing it from the request means `POST /orders` would no longer require `channel`.",
